{"title":"Career Roadmap — NGO Program Officer","role":"NGO Program Officer","summary":"Role overview:\nAn NGO Program Officer supports the design, implementation, monitoring and reporting of development programmes. With a Human Development/Early Childhood Development background, the strongest pathway is through child development, education, nutrition, early childhood care, family support, community development and child-protection programmes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Human Development / Early Childhood Development"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"NGO internship + community project"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Programme implementation + M&E"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Programme management + fundraising"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Development leadership + social-impact strategy"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The role combines programme implementation","community engagement","monitoring & evaluation","documentation","stakeholder coordination","basic data analysis."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Human Development/Early Childhood Development","NGO/Development Internship","Program Associate/Project Assistant","Program Officer","Senior Program Officer","Program Manager","Program Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strong alignment, particularly for NGOs working with children, families, education, nutrition and community development."},{"type":"note","label":"Timeline assumption","text":"The student starts UG in 2026. B.Sc duration may be 3 or 4 years depending on the university."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","P